From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DE25-Nano Port <de25-nano@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Allow DE25 remote command writes

Main creates its command FIFO with mode 0666, but the service umask reduces it
to 0644. Restore the intended mode explicitly on DE25 so the SSH account can
request Menu display, status capture, and compatibility-checked core loads
without root privileges.
---
 input.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/input.cpp b/input.cpp
index 955fb53..072492a 100644
--- a/input.cpp
+++ b/input.cpp
@@ -5140,5 +5140,12 @@ int input_test(int getchar)
 		unlink(CMD_FIFO);
 		mkfifo(CMD_FIFO, 0666);
+#ifdef MISTER_DE25
+		// The service umask otherwise reduces the requested 0666 mode to 0644,
+		// preventing the unprivileged SSH account from issuing remote Menu,
+		// status, and core-load commands.
+		if (chmod(CMD_FIFO, 0666))
+			printf("Unable to make %s remotely writable: %s\n", CMD_FIFO, strerror(errno));
+#endif
 
 		pool[NUMDEV+1].fd = open(CMD_FIFO, O_RDWR | O_NONBLOCK | O_CLOEXEC);
 		pool[NUMDEV+1].events = POLLIN;
